{
  "_doc": "WHICH PRODUCT A FULL AD SHOWS WHEN NOBODY PICKED IT, and how often. The owner, 2026-11-18: 'why are the same elements being used on the hero... same phones.. or same ipad arrangements.. we need infinite but prioritized by recent popular and expensive models', 'not just front and back', 'any possible style.. side profile... front with lock screens.. backs.. diagonal.. multi.. or just 1', 'all colors too ..', 'but obviously the most will be the hot in demand models'. Read by scripts/build_product_demand.mjs, which writes motion/product-demand.js (the site cannot read spec/: netlify.toml 404s it), and by scripts/build_full_subjects.mjs, which writes each line's pool into motion/subjects.json. Weights are relative within a line; a model or picture not listed weighs the line's rest. They are set by launch year and price tier (Pro Max over Pro over the base model over e and mini; the newest year first), steep on purpose (the owner: 'the most will be the hot in demand models'): on the iPhone line the five newest Pro and Pro Max models are about three sets in four, not by sales counts the studio does not have: when the shop's own quote or purchase counts exist, they replace these numbers. A customer's own pick (phones chosen in Phones, a picture chosen with Picture) is never overridden. To change what shows most, change a number here and run both scripts.",
  "version": "2026-11-23",
